From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdb/nat: no-MMU Linux without uClibc

The ptrace feature probe's CLONE_VM child is GDB's no-MMU path, and it
is taken only for uClibc.  A no-MMU kernel's compiler defines
__uClinux__ whatever the C library, and musl's fork() fails without an
MMU, so take it for __uClinux__ too.  fork_inferior already uses vfork.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

diff --git a/gdb/nat/linux-ptrace.c b/gdb/nat/linux-ptrace.c
index 43c2d3a..9748fec 100644
--- a/gdb/nat/linux-ptrace.c
+++ b/gdb/nat/linux-ptrace.c
@@ -317,7 +317,7 @@ linux_fork_to_function (gdb_byte *child_stack, int (*function) (void *))
   /* Sanity check the function pointer.  */
   gdb_assert (function != NULL);
 
-#if defined(__UCLIBC__) && defined(HAS_NOMMU)
+#if defined(HAS_NOMMU)
 #define STACK_SIZE 4096
 
     if (child_stack == NULL)
diff --git a/gdb/nat/linux-ptrace.h b/gdb/nat/linux-ptrace.h
index 6cf5c80..f1b3227 100644
--- a/gdb/nat/linux-ptrace.h
+++ b/gdb/nat/linux-ptrace.h
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@
 #include <asm/ptrace.h>
 #define HAS_NOMMU
 #endif
+#elif defined(__uClinux__)
+#define HAS_NOMMU
 #endif
 
 #if !defined(PTRACE_TYPE_ARG3)
